{"name":"Desert Fortress","hex":"#d3bdac","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"desert","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A barren area of land or desolate terrain, especially one with little water or vegetation; a wasteland.\n\nIn particular, a barren, arid area of land which is hot, with sandy, rocky, or parched ground.","In particular, a barren, arid area of land which is hot, with sandy, rocky, or parched ground."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Usually of a place: abandoned, deserted, or uninhabited."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/desert"},{"term":"fortress","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A fortified place; a large and permanent fortification, sometimes including a town; for example a fort, a castle; a stronghold; a place of defense or security.","A position that, if obtained by the weaker side, will prevent penetration by the opposing side, generally achieving a draw."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To furnish with a fortress or with fortresses; to guard, to fortify."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fortress"}],"entries":[{"title":"Desert","blocks":[{"text":"A desert is a landscape where little precipitation occurs and, consequently, living conditions create unique biomes and ecosystems. The lack of vegetation exposes the unprotected surface of the ground to denudation. About one-third of the land surface of the Earth is arid or semi-arid. This includes much of the polar regions, where little precipitation occurs, and which are sometimes called polar deserts or \"cold deserts\". Deserts can be classified by the amount of precipitation that falls, by the temperature that prevails, by the causes of desertification or by their geographical location."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Rub_al_Khali_002.JPG/330px-Rub_al_Khali_002.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Desert","wikidata":"Q8514"},{"title":"Fortification","blocks":[{"text":"A fortification is a military construction designed for the defense of territories in warfare, and is used to establish rule in a region during peacetime. The term is derived from Latin fortis (\"strong\") and facere."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Castillo_San_Felipe_del_Morro_%2810_of_1%29.jpg/330px-Castillo_San_Felipe_del_Morro_%2810_of_1%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fortification","wikidata":"Q57821"},{"title":"Desert sand (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Desert sand is a very light and very weakly saturated reddish yellow color which corresponds specifically to the coloration of sand. It may also be regarded as a deep tone of beige."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Sossusvlei_Dune_Namib_Desert_Namibia_Luca_Galuzzi_2004.JPG/330px-Sossusvlei_Dune_Namib_Desert_Namibia_Luca_Galuzzi_2004.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Desert_sand_(color)","wikidata":"Q9303163"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Groupe_de_dromadaire_avec_son_chamelier_dans_le_sud_tunisien.jpg/500px-Groupe_de_dromadaire_avec_son_chamelier_dans_le_sud_tunisien.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Groupe_de_dromadaire_avec_son_chamelier_dans_le_sud_tunisien.jpg/1280px-Groupe_de_dromadaire_avec_son_chamelier_dans_le_sud_tunisien.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Groupe_de_dromadaire_avec_son_chamelier_dans_le_sud_tunisien.jpg/500px-Groupe_de_dromadaire_avec_son_chamelier_dans_le_sud_tunisien.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail